course: dictionary
lesson: 15572
title: Sustained: going on and getting hurt
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sustained comes from the verb sustain. Its most common meaning is kept going for a long time without stopping. «She showed sustained effort, practising her piano every day for a whole year.» The word effort tells you something is being done, and sustained tells you it did not stop.
explain: Sustain has more than one meaning. In formal writing, to sustain an injury means to be hurt. «The footballer sustained a knee injury in the second half.» The word injury is the clue: it is about being hurt, so sustained means got or suffered.
explain: Sustain can also mean to keep something alive or hold up its weight. «Water and sunlight sustain plants.» The clue is the way the words link: plants need these things to stay alive, so sustain means keep alive. Try swapping in keep going, keep alive, or got hurt, and see which one fits the sentence.
fact: Sustained is an adjective when it describes a noun, as in «sustained effort».
fact: Sustained is also the past form of the verb sustain: «The bridge sustained heavy damage in the storm.»
fact: «Sustained» means kept going for a long time without stopping.
fact: «Sustained» in «sustained an injury» means was hurt, and this is a formal use.
fact: «Sustain» can mean to keep something alive or to hold up its weight, as in «food sustains life».
exercise: «The sustained rain made the river rise all week.» What does sustained mean here? | *Kept going for a long time without stopping | Stopped at once | Very quick and sudden | Warm and sunny
exercise: «The boxer sustained a cut above his eye.» What does sustained mean here? | Was very happy | Won the fight easily | *Was hurt
exercise: «Plants need sunlight and water, which sustain them.» Which word means about the same as sustain here? | Break | Paint | *Keep alive | Forget
test: «Her sustained attack on the castle lasted all night.» What does sustained mean here? | Kept going for a long time without stopping | Stopped suddenly | Very quiet | *Kept going for a long time without stopping, as in a steady attack
test: «He sustained a small injury, but he kept his sustained effort going.» Which meaning fits the first sustained? | *Was hurt, from the words small injury | Was hurt | Ran fast | Shouted loudly
exam: «The runner's sustained effort carried her to the finish, even though she sustained a small blister.» In the first part, what does sustained mean? | *Kept going for a long time without stopping | Stopped suddenly | Painted | Was hurt
